BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3d809cfd69f2@civicswa
DTSTAMP:20261111T163557Z
DTSTART:20261119T020000Z
DTEND:20261119T075900Z
SUMMARY:JOINT HEARING OF THE EAST WENATCHEE PLANNING COMMISSION AND DOUGLAS COUNTY PLANNING COMMISSION – CONTINUED FROM OCTOBER 28TH (Douglas County)
LOCATION:City of East Wenatchee and Douglas County Joint Planning Commission meeting on November 18\, 2026\, is a continuation of the October 28\, 2026\, public hearing on Greater East Wenatchee Comprehensive Plan (including East Wenatchee Urban Growth Area)\, with corresponding amendments to zoning maps and development regulations. AGENDA Wednesday\, November 18\, 2026 - 6:00 PM East Wenatchee City Hall\, Council Chambers 271 9th Street NE\, East Wenatchee\, WA The hearing will be conducted in person with an Zoom option. To join using Zoom\, please use this URL: https://us02web.zoom.us/j/81035562054 Or phone number 1-253-215-8782. Meeting ID: 810 3556 2054. Public Testimony will be limited to three minutes. If there are many speakers\, a representative may be appointed to speak on behalf of the group. I. CALL TO ORDER II. ADMINISTRATIVE PROCEDURES A. None III. CITIZEN COMMENT: The Citizen Comment period is to provide the opportunity for members of the public to address the planning commission on a topic not on the agenda. The Chair will ask if there are any citizens wishing to address the Commission. When recognized please step up to the microphone\, give your name and mailing address\, and state the matter of interest. Citizen comments will be limited to three minutes. IV. OLD BUSINESS A. None V. NEW BUSINESS A. Continued Public Hearing Hearing procedures A joint city/county public hearing continued from October 28th to consider amendments to the Greater East Wenatchee Area Comprehensive Plan\, EWMC Title 17 Zoning\, DCC Title 18A East Wenatchee UGA Zoning\, and EWMC Title 19.11 Definitions. Comprehensive plan amendments include text amendments\, map amendments and an expansion of the East Wenatchee Urban Growth Boundary. Development regulation amendments include housing related changes and adoption of zoning maps that correspond to the land use designation map in the comprehensive plan. VI. OTHER BUSINESS A. None VII. ADJOURNMENT - 271 NE 9th Street East Wenatchee WA 98802
URL:/common/modules/iCalendar/iCalendar.aspx?feed=calendar&catID=14
END:VEVENT
